{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/611849-is-malfeas-unbeatable","id":611849,"title":"Is Malfeas unbeatable?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-01T21:24:00-07:00","id":611849,"title":"Is Malfeas unbeatable?","content":"So it turns out the Wyrm let the Garou steal Queen Ananassa's prison rather than the raid on Malfeas being an extremely costly victory for the Garou back when they were at full power. Is this proof that there are no true victories when they are fought on the Wyrm's home turf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T22:40:13-07:00","id":611895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/611849-is-malfeas-unbeatable#post611849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it turns out the Wyrm let the Garou steal Queen Ananassa's prison rather than the raid on Malfeas being an extremely costly victory for the Garou back when they were at full power. Is this proof that there are no true victories when they are fought on the Wyrm's home turf?</div> </div> </div> </div>The 20th Book of the Wyrm talks about plenty of ways the Garou can strike out against their enemies within Malfeas. Killing Maeljin Incarna isn't easy, but the book lists some ways to do it, as well as ways to collapse the entrance to the Black Spiral itself. Malfeas is not a homogenous place, and though it is the stronghold of the Wyrm, there are certainly targets within it that the Garou can eliminate/sabotage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T11:59:01-07:00","id":612476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/611849-is-malfeas-unbeatable?p=611895#post611895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The 20th Book of the Wyrm talks about plenty of ways the Garou can strike out against their enemies within Malfeas. Killing Maeljin Incarna isn't easy, but the book lists some ways to do it, as well as ways to collapse the entrance to the Black Spiral itself. Malfeas is not a homogenous place, and though it is the stronghold of the Wyrm, there are certainly targets within it that the Garou can eliminate/sabotage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just don't stay there too long at one time. BotW20 states &quot;A traveler who remains in Malfeas for more than a day begins hearing foul whispers. He can see patches of his skin or fur turn grey and sickly. If he escapes before these afflictions finish warping his mind and body, he will heal within a week or two. While he remains in Malfeas, however, no known force can quiet the whispers or restore his degraded flesh. Should he be unlucky enough to remain in Malfeas for more than three months, the whispers will accompany him long after his departure from the realm. His entire skin and fur becomes grey and withered looking, and the transformation does not heal when he leaves. Only powerful healing rites can cure these taints (see \u201cTaint,\u201d p. 179). Almost everyone who spends more than three months in Malfeas suffers from a long-standing mental or physical taint, and a few unfortunates suffer from both.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is a fine defense against permanent Gaian resistance groups trying to operate in Malfeas, IMHO. Stay too long and you become the enemy. Brrrr....<br /> <br /> Of course, you can always stay in Malfeas for less than three months, go back to your home sept, get a Rite of Cleansing (or other appropriate Rite) done on you and return to Malfeas to continue the fight. That's one hell of a guerrilla campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 08-03-2015, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:35:40-07:00","id":616058,"title":"","content":"It's probably a waste of time to actually keep fighting in Malfeas. There are so many targets that are much more pressing and where the effect of the Garou will be quite a bit more noticeable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T01:35:47-07:00","id":616086,"title":"","content":"Still, it would be interesting to see on a chronicle the attempt at a permanent base of operation in Malfeas, with Garou assigned for two months stays and a &quot;nearby&quot; sept outside cleansing the ones who get out. a week of respite and they are ready to go again, until they retire from this assignment to go with honor to their original septs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T12:03:46-07:00","id":616733,"title":"","content":"That could be really compelling, but you just know it's not going to end well, or anything remotely like well. It would be a dramatic and unexpected twist if it _didn't_ take a huge chunk out of the Garou Nation when it all went to hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T20:18:20-07:00","id":618363,"title":"","content":"It <u>could</u> work in a chronicle set on course for Apocalypse anyway.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, what would be the fun if it <b>didn't</b> went to Hell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}